Research decision memo — Stage 1
Title: Agent-Based Econophysics as an Equilibrium Computation Method
Status: NOT STARTED

Central hypothesis: Can many-agent simulations of policy-optimal decisions replicate the stationary and transition distributions of the same heterogeneous-agent general equilibrium model?

Feasibility prior:
Yes as a numerical representation, provided the simulated decision rules solve the same equilibrium and common/aggregate risk is consistently forecast.

Core economic distinction:
Distributional operator solution of Stage 0 at the same prices and shocks

Conditions to check:
1. Discrete Kolmogorov or histogram distribution evolution
2. Law of motion of aggregate states
3. Market-clearing identities in agent simulation

Pass / fail criterion:
Treat ABM as an implementation method, not as a free-standing economic microfoundation.

The project reports negative feasibility results when a kinetic, entropy, adaptive-trading, or heuristic-firm mechanism cannot be reconciled with optimization and equilibrium. Do not silently weaken rational expectations or drop clearing equations.

Evidence status: no derived theorems, numerical solutions or validated simulations committed yet.
